changes the bases of the free modules in a way which is not invertible (over
ZZ) when the ground field has positive characteristic.


Version 2.0 overhaul.  This release extends the original PieriMaps package in
three respects:
  * Multiple basis conventions. Every map can be expressed in the package's
    original convention (default Convention => "Row"), the column-form Filling
    basis from *note SchurFunctors: (SchurFunctors)Top, (Convention =>
    "Filling"), or the divided-power Weyl-module basis (Convention => "Weyl").
    See *note Convention: Convention,.
  * Both directions of every map. In addition to the inclusion direction (*note
    pieri: pieri,, *note pieriColumn: pieriColumn,, *note lrMap: lrMap,), the
    projection direction is provided via *note dualPieri: dualPieri,, *note
    dualPieriColumn: dualPieriColumn,, and *note dualLR: dualLR,.  Each pair
    satisfies $\mathrm{dual} \circ \mathrm{incl} = \mathrm{Id}$, the canonical
    $GL$-equivariant projection given by Schur's lemma.
  * Verifications. *note verifyEquivariant: verifyEquivariant, checks
    $GL_n$-equivariance of any matrix between Schur modules via the
    Chevalley-generator commutativity test; *note verifyWellDefined:
    verifyWellDefined, checks compatibility with the Garnir relations of the
    chosen convention.
Examples.


The single-box Pieri inclusion $S_{(2,1)} V \to V \otimes S_{(1,1)} V$ in three
variables.  Each row of symbolicForm displays a source standard tableau on the
left and its image as a sum of (target tableau, coefficient) pairs on the
right:
+-------------------------------+
|i36 : R = QQ[a,b,c];           |
+-------------------------------+
|i37 : M = pieri({2,1}, {1}, R);|
|                               |
|              3      8         |
|o37 : Matrix R  <-- R          |
+-------------------------------+
|i38 : symbolicForm M           |
|                               |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|       +-+|       |
|o38 = ||0|0||2a  *  |0||       |
|      ||1| ||       |1||       |
|      |+-+-+|       +-+|       |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|       +-+|       |
|      ||0|0||2a  *  |0||       |
|      ||2| ||       |2||       |
|      |+-+-+|       +-+|       |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      ||0|1||b  *  |0| |       |
|      ||1| ||      |1| |       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      ||0|1||b  *  |0| |       |
|      ||2| ||      |2| |       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      |     |      +-+ |       |
|      |     |a  *  |1| |       |
|      |     |      |2| |       |
|      |     |      +-+ |       |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      ||0|2||c  *  |0| |       |
|      ||1| ||      |1| |       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      |     |       +-+|       |
|      |     |-a  *  |1||       |
|      |     |       |2||       |
|      |     |       +-+|       |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      ||0|2||c  *  |0| |       |
|      ||2| ||      |2| |       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|       +-+|       |
|      ||1|1||2b  *  |1||       |
|      ||2| ||       |2||       |
|      |+-+-+|       +-+|       |
|      +-----+----------+       |
|      |+-+-+|      +-+ |       |
|      ||1|2||c  *  |1| |       |
