The same map in the column-form (Filling) convention is the literal change of
basis.  Both matrices are equivariant injections and have the same rank:
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i39 : R = QQ[a,b,c];                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i40 : Mrow = pieri({2,1}, {1}, R, Convention => "Row");    |
|                                                           |
|              3      8                                     |
|o40 : Matrix R  <-- R                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i41 : Mfil = pieri({2,1}, {1}, R, Convention => "Filling");|
|                                                           |
|              3      8                                     |
|o41 : Matrix R  <-- R                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i42 : (rank Mrow, rank Mfil)                               |
|                                                           |
|o42 = (3, 3)                                               |
|                                                           |
|o42 : Sequence                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
The projection *note dualPieri: dualPieri, left-inverts *note pieri: pieri,.
Verified by $\mathrm{dualPieri} \circ \mathrm{applyPieri}(T_\mu) = T_\mu$ on
the highest-weight vector:
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i43 : R = QQ[a,b,c];                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i44 : Tmu = (standardTableaux(3, {2,1}))#0;                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i45 : img = applyPieri(({2,1}, {1}), Tmu, R);                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i46 : back = flatten for term in img list applyDualPieri(({2,1}, {1}),       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|term#0, term#1, 3);                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i47 : back                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o47 = {{1, {{0, 0}, {1}}}}                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o47 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
When the Littlewood-Richardson coefficient $c^\lambda_{\mu,\nu}$ exceeds 1,
distinct LR tableaux $Q$ produce $c$ linearly independent inclusions $\Psi_Q :
S_\lambda V \hookrightarrow S_\nu V \otimes S_\mu V$:
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i48 : Qs = lrTableaux({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1});  -- c^{(3,2,1)}_{(2,1),(2,1)} =|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|2                                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i49 : M1 = lrMap(({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1}), Qs#0, 3);                          |
|                                                                             |
|               64       8                                                    |
|o49 : Matrix QQ   <-- QQ                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i50 : M2 = lrMap(({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1}), Qs#1, 3);                          |
|                                                                             |
|               64       8                                                    |
|o50 : Matrix QQ   <-- QQ                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i51 : rank(M1 | M2) == 16    -- 2 * dim S_{(3,2,1)} -- linearly independent  |
|                                                                             |
|o51 = true                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
Each *note dualLR: dualLR, projects onto exactly its own $Q$-summand and
annihilates the others:
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i52 : Qs = lrTableaux({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1});     |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i53 : M0 = lrMap(({3,2,1},{2,1},{2,1}), Qs#0, 3); |
|                                                  |
|               64       8                         |
|o53 : Matrix QQ   <-- QQ                          |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i54 : M1 = lrMap(({3,2,1},{2,1},{2,1}), Qs#1, 3); |
|                                                  |
|               64       8                         |
|o54 : Matrix QQ   <-- QQ                          |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i55 : N0 = dualLR(({3,2,1},{2,1},{2,1}), Qs#0, 3);|
|                                                  |
|               8       64                         |
|o55 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                           |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i56 : N0 * M0 == id_(QQ^(numColumns M0))          |
|                                                  |
|o56 = true                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i57 : N0 * M1 == 0                                |
|                                                  |
|o57 = true                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+
*note verifyEquivariant: verifyEquivariant, checks Chevalley-generator
commutativity for any matrix between Schur reps -- a direct $GL_n$-equivariance
test:
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i58 : R = QQ[a,b,c];                                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i59 : M = pieri({3,2,1}, {2}, R);   -- inclusion at the interior row|
|                                                                    |
|              6      8                                              |
|o59 : Matrix R  <-- R                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i60 : verifyEquivariant(M, {3,2,1}, {2}, R)                         |
|                                                                    |
|o60 = true                                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
And *note verifyWellDefined: verifyWellDefined, confirms that an LR map factors
through the Garnir relations of the chosen convention:
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i61 : Qs = lrTableaux({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1});          |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i62 : verifyWellDefined(({3,2,1},{2,1},{2,1}), Qs#0, 3,|
|      Convention => "Filling", Verbose => false)       |
|                                                       |
|o62 = true                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i63 :                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

