applyDualPieri -- apply dualPieri to a single basis pair (poly, T_lambda)
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        applyDualPieri((mu, boxes), poly, T, n)
        applyDualPieri(..., Convention => "Row" | "Filling" | "Weyl")
  * Inputs:
      * (mu, boxes), a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, the same data
        passed to *note dualPieri: dualPieri,
      * poly, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a homogeneous
        polynomial of degree $d = \#\mathrm{boxes}$ in the polynomial ring P
        (an element of $\mathrm{Sym}^d V$)
      * T, a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, a tableau of shape
        $\lambda$.  Accepted as either a List or a Filling.  In "Row"/"Weyl"
        convention a List is the PM row form; in "Filling" convention a List is
        column form (auto-wrapped).  A Filling is always treated as column
        form.  Non-standard inputs are straightened first using the
        convention's relations.
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, $\dim V$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Convention => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "Row", , basis for source $S_\lambda$ and target $S_\mu$.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of pairs {coefficient, T_mu}
        representing the image as a sum $\sum c_i \cdot T_\mu^{(i)}$ in $S_\mu
        V$.  Zero coefficients are dropped.

Description
===========

Convenience wrapper for *note dualPieri: dualPieri,: evaluates the projection
on a single source basis vector $\mathrm{poly} \otimes T_\lambda$ and returns a
sparse representation of its image.  Useful for hand-checks and interactive
exploration when the full *note dualPieri: dualPieri, matrix is too large.


Input flexibility: T may be in either tableau type.  For Convention => "Row", a
Filling input is converted via *note fillingToPM: fillingToPM, before
straightening; for Convention => "Filling", a List input is converted via *note
pmToFilling: pmToFilling,.  Non-standard tableaux straighten first.
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = QQ[a,b,c];                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Tlam = {{0,0},{1}};   -- standard PM tableau of {2,1}|
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : applyDualPieri(({3,1}, {1}), a, Tlam, 3)             |
|                                                          |
|       1                                                  |
|o3 = {{-, {{0, 0, 0}, {1}}}}                              |
|       3                                                  |
|                                                          |
|o3 : List                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : -- Non-standard input is straightened first (row-Garnir).|
|     P = QQ[a,b,c,d];                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : applyDualPieri(({3,2,1}, {3}), a, {{1,0},{2}}, 4)        |
|                                                              |
|o5 = {}                                                       |
|                                                              |
|o5 : List                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 :                                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

