applyLR -- apply Psi_Q to a single tableau of shape lambda
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        applyLR((lambda, mu, nu), Q, T, n)
        applyLR(..., Convention => "Row" | "Filling" | "Weyl")
  * Inputs:
      * (lambda, mu, nu), a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, three
        partitions specifying the LR map
      * Q, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, an LR tableau as returned by
        *note lrTableaux: lrTableaux,
      * T, a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, a tableau of shape
        $\lambda$.  May be supplied as a List or as a Filling.  In "Row"/"Weyl"
        convention a List is interpreted as PM row form; in "Filling"
        convention a List is interpreted as column form (and wrapped
        automatically). A Filling is always treated as column form. T need not
        be standard; it is straightened internally using the convention's
        straightening relations.
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the dimension of $V$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Convention => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "Row", , basis convention used to interpret T and label the output
        $T_\nu$, $T_\mu$.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of triples {c, T_nu, T_mu}
        representing the image as the sum $\sum c_i \cdot T_\nu^{(i)} \otimes
        T_\mu^{(i)}$ in $S_\nu V \otimes S_\mu V$

Description
===========

Computes the image of a single basis vector (or, more generally, of any
tableau, which is first straightened into the SSYT basis of $S_\lambda V$)
under the LR inclusion $\Psi_Q$.  The output is intended for human reading or
interactive exploration when the full *note lrMap: lrMap, matrix is too large
to display.  Use *note displayLRImage: displayLRImage, for pretty-printing.


When Convention => "Filling" is chosen, the input T must be a SchurFunctors
Filling, and the output uses Fillings on both target sides.  Straightening uses
SchurFunctors' column-Garnir relations.  When Convention => "Row" or "Weyl", T
is a list of rows and PieriMaps' row-Garnir straightening is applied.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Qs = lrTableaux({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1});                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : T = {{0,0,0},{1,1},{2}};   -- highest-weight vector of S_(3,2,1) QQ^3   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : applyLR(({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1}), Qs#0, T, 3)                            |
|                                                                             |
|       27                                                                    |
|o3 = {{--, {{0, 0}, {1}}, {{0, 1}, {2}, {}}}, {9, {{0, 0}, {1}}, {{0, 2},    |
|        4                                                                    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                   63                                        9               |
|     {1}, {}}}, {- --, {{0, 0}, {2}}, {{0, 1}, {1}, {}}}, {- -, {{0, 1},     |
|                    4                                        2               |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                27                                        9  |
|     {1}}, {{0, 0}, {2}, {}}}, {--, {{0, 1}, {2}}, {{0, 0}, {1}, {}}}, {- -, |
|                                 4                                        4  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {{0, 2}, {1}}, {{0, 0}, {1}, {}}}}                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : displayLRImage applyLR(({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1}), Qs#0, T, 3)             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 =   +  27/4 . [1 1 ] ⊗ [1 2 ]                                             |
|                  2        3                                                 |
|       +  9 . [1 1 ] ⊗ [1 3 ]                                                |
|               2        2                                                    |
|       -  63/4 . [1 1 ] ⊗ [1 2 ]                                             |
|                  3        2                                                 |
|       -  9/2 . [1 2 ] ⊗ [1 1 ]                                              |
|                 2        3                                                  |
|       +  27/4 . [1 2 ] ⊗ [1 1 ]                                             |
|                  3        2                                                 |
|       -  9/4 . [1 3 ] ⊗ [1 1 ]                                              |
|                 2        2                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : -- Non-standard input: row-Garnir straightening before applying.        |
|     Tnonstd = {{1,0},{2}};   -- row 0 not weakly-increasing                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : applyLR(({2,1}, {1}, {1,1}), (lrTableaux({2,1},{1},{1,1}))#0, Tnonstd,  |
|                                                                             |
|       3                           3                                         |
|o6 = {{-, {{0}, {2}}, {{1}, {}}}, {-, {{1}, {2}}, {{0}, {}}}}                |
|       2                           2                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3)                                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 :                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

