Convention -- tableau basis convention used by PieriMaps' overhauled functions
******************************************************************************

Description
===========

An option accepted by *note pieri: pieri,, *note lrMap: lrMap,, *note applyLR:
applyLR,, *note pureFree: pureFree,, and *note verifyWellDefined:
verifyWellDefined,.  Possible values:
  * "Row" (default): the original PieriMaps row-form basis.  Source/target
    Schur modules are indexed by SSYTs as lists of weakly-increasing rows.
  * "Filling": the SchurFunctors column-form basis.  Source/target are indexed
    by Fillings, with column-Garnir straightening relations.  The matrix is
    obtained by post-hoc basis change with the equivariant iso *note
    pmToFilling: pmToFilling,.
  * "Weyl": the divided-power row-form basis.  Source/target are indexed by
    WeylFillings.  Numerically the same data as the Row matrix; it is just that
    the bases are interpreted on the Weyl (divided-power) side rather than the
    Schur side.
Use *note verifyWellDefined: verifyWellDefined, to verify that the
chosen-convention map respects the appropriate straightening relations.
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = QQ[a,b,c];                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : pieri({2,1}, {1}, P, Convention => "Row")    |
|                                                  |
|o2 = | 2a 0  b 0 c  0 0  0 |                      |
|     | 0  2a 0 b 0  c 0  0 |                      |
|     | 0  0  0 a -a 0 2b c |                      |
|                                                  |
|             3      8                             |
|o2 : Matrix P  <-- P                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : pieri({2,1}, {1}, P, Convention => "Filling")|
|                                                  |
|o3 = | 3/2a 3/2b c     0    1/2c 0    0    0    | |
|     | 0    0    1/2b  3/2a b    3/2c 0    0    | |
|     | 0    0    -1/2a 0    1/2a 0    3/2b 3/2c | |
|                                                  |
|             3      8                             |
|o3 : Matrix P  <-- P                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+

