fillingToPM -- convert a SchurFunctors column-form Filling to PieriMaps row-form tableaux
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        fillingToPM F
  * Inputs:
      * F, Filling, a SchurFunctors column-form Filling
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, the image of F under the
        antisymmetrize-then-symmetrize equivariant map $\wedge^{\lambda'} V \to
        \mathrm{Sym}^\lambda V$, expressed as a sum of standard PM-form
        tableaux with rational coefficients (after PieriMaps straightening).

Description
===========

Inverse (up to a uniform scalar) of *note pmToFilling: pmToFilling,.  Each
column of F is wedge-expanded into $V^{\otimes |\lambda|}$ via the column
antisymmetrizer (signed sum over permutations, with normalization $1/\prod
\lambda'_j!$), reordered by rows, and projected to symmetric (sort) per row.
The result is straightened into the standard PM basis.
+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage "SchurFunctors";    |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = new Filling from {{0,2},{1}};|
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : fillingToPM F                    |
|                                      |
|o3 = HashTable{{{0, 1}, {2}} => 1}    |
|                                1     |
|               {{0, 2}, {1}} => -     |
|                                2     |
|                                      |
|o3 : HashTable                        |
+--------------------------------------+

