pureFree -- computes a GL(V)-equivariant map whose resolution is pure, or the reduction mod p of such a map
***********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        pureFree(d, P)
        pureFree(d, P, Convention => "Row" | "Filling" | "Weyl")
  * Inputs:
      * d, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of degrees (increasing
        numbers)
      * P, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, a polynomial
        ring over a field $K$ in $n$ variables
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Convention => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "Row", , basis convention used internally by *note pieri: pieri,.
        Defaults to "Row"; the resulting Betti table does not depend on the
        choice.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, A map whose cokernel has Betti
        diagram with degree sequence $d$ if $K$ has characteristic 0.  If $K$
        has positive characteristic $p$, then the corresponding map is
        calculated over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is lifted to a $\mathbb{Z}$-form which
        is then reduced mod $p$.

Description
===========

The function translates the data of a degree sequence $d$ for a desired pure
free resolution into the data of a Pieri map according to the formula of
Eisenbud-Fl\o ystad-Weyman and then applies the function *note pieri: pieri,.
The Convention option is forwarded to that internal Pieri call so that the
resulting matrix is presented in the user's preferred basis convention; the
Betti table of the resulting resolution is the same in all conventions.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : betti res coker pureFree({0,1,2,4}, QQ[a,b,c]) -- degree sequence       |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2 3                                                          |
|o1 = total: 3 8 6 1                                                          |
|         0: 3 8 6 .                                                          |
|         1: . . . 1                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : BettiTally                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{0,1,2,4}                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : betti res coker pureFree({0,1,2,4}, ZZ/2[a,b,c]) -- same map, but       |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2 3                                                          |
|o2 = total: 3 8 6 1                                                          |
|         0: 3 8 6 .                                                          |
|         1: . . . 1                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : BettiTally                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|reduced mod 2                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : betti res coker pureFree({0,1,2,4}, GF(4)[a,b,c]) -- can also use non   |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2 3                                                          |
|o3 = total: 3 8 6 1                                                          |
|         0: 3 8 6 .                                                          |
|         1: . . . 1                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : BettiTally                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|prime fields                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : -- The Betti table is independent of the chosen convention:             |
|     P = QQ[a,b,c];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : bettiR = betti res coker pureFree({0,1,2,4}, P, Convention => "Row");   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : bettiF = betti res coker pureFree({0,1,2,4}, P, Convention =>           |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|"Filling");                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : bettiR == bettiF                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 :                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

