verifyEquivariant -- rigorously verify GL_n-equivariance of a Schur-rep matrix
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        verifyEquivariant(M, mu, boxes, P)               -- pieri-type inclusion
        verifyEquivariant(M, shapes, n)                  -- lrMap-type inclusion
        verifyEquivariant(M, mu, boxes, P, Direction => "Dual")  -- dualPieri-type projection
        verifyEquivariant(M, shapes, n, Direction => "Dual")     -- dualLR-type projection
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the matrix to test for
        $GL_n$-equivariance
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Convention => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "Row", , basis convention used by M's rows and columns.  Default "Row".
      * Verbose => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, , if true print the first failing $(i, j, T)$ when the test
        fails.  Default false.
      * Direction => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value
        "Inclusion", , "Inclusion" (default) or "Dual" to indicate the
        direction of the map.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if M commutes with
        every Chevalley generator $E_{i,j}$ of $\mathfrak{gl}_n$ ($i \neq j$);
        false otherwise

Description
===========

Tests whether a matrix M between Schur-functor representations is genuinely
$GL_n$-equivariant by checking that $M \circ \rho_{\mathrm{src}}(E_{i,j}) =
\rho_{\mathrm{tgt}}(E_{i,j}) \circ M$ for every Chevalley generator $E_{i,j}$.
Since the $E_{i,j}$ ($i \neq j$) generate the strictly upper- and strictly
lower-triangular parts of $\mathfrak{gl}_n$, and our matrices commute with the
diagonal automatically (entries are weight-homogeneous), commutativity with all
$E_{i,j}$ is equivalent to full $GL_n$-equivariance.


Action conventions: $E_{i,j}$ acts on $V = K^n$ by $x_l \mapsto \delta_{l,j}\,
x_i$ (i.e. the differential operator $x_i\, \partial/\partial x_j$ on
polynomials), on a Schur module $S_\lambda V$ by replacing each entry equal to
$j$ with $i$ in a tableau (summed over positions, then straightened), and on a
tensor product by Leibniz.


Four overloads cover the maps in this package:
  * verifyEquivariant(M, mu, boxes, P) -- $M \colon S_\mu V \to \mathrm{Sym}^d
    V \otimes S_\lambda V$ (or $\wedge^d V$ for skew-commutative P), the
    inclusion produced by *note pieri: pieri, or *note pieriColumn:
    pieriColumn,.
  * verifyEquivariant(M, (lambda, mu, nu), n) -- $M \colon S_\lambda V \to
    S_\nu V \otimes S_\mu V$, the inclusion produced by *note lrMap: lrMap,.
  * verifyEquivariant(M, mu, boxes, P, Direction => "Dual") -- $M \colon
    \mathrm{Sym}^d V \otimes S_\lambda V \to S_\mu V$, the projection produced
    by *note dualPieri: dualPieri,.
  * verifyEquivariant(M, (lambda, mu, nu), n, Direction => "Dual") -- $M \colon
    S_\nu V \otimes S_\mu V \to S_\lambda V$, the projection produced by *note
    dualLR: dualLR,.
+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = QQ[a,b,c];                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = pieri({3,2,1}, {2}, P);          |
|                                          |
|             6      8                     |
|o2 : Matrix P  <-- P                      |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : verifyEquivariant(M, {3,2,1}, {2}, P)|
|                                          |
|o3 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : P = QQ[a,b,c];   -- verify the dual Pieri projection      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = dualPieri({3,2,1}, {2}, P);                           |
|                                                               |
|              8       18                                       |
|o5 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : verifyEquivariant(N, {3,2,1}, {2}, P, Direction => "Dual")|
|                                                               |
|o6 = true                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Q = (lrTableaux({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1}))#0;  -- multiplicity-2 LR        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|inclusion                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : M = lrMap(({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1}), Q, 3);                               |
|                                                                             |
|              64       8                                                     |
|o8 : Matrix QQ   <-- QQ                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : verifyEquivariant(M, ({3,2,1}, {2,1}, {2,1}), 3)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

